{"action":"final","query":{"op":"none","id":null,"start":null,"end":null,"search":null,"groupBy":null},"diagnosis":"getLiveIntervals follows descriptor views but stops at arith.select, so backing allocations can expire before the selected descriptor's final use. In case-24/25, the temporary occupies columns [0,64), overlapping both selected sources; selected outputs become 7 (fact-24/26). The 32-column contrast isolates the overlap: case-26 passes when selecting [32,64), while case-27 fails when selecting [0,32) (fact-27/29). Early allocation controls case-30/31 pass with the temporary at column 64 (fact-33/35). Case-32 also demonstrates legal reuse of the dead second allocation (fact-36/37). Extend the existing traversal through select results, transitively covering chained selects and views; deduplicate visited operations to avoid repeated traversal of converging chains. Allocation sizes, alignment, row constraints, first-fit policy, and lifetime-based reuse remain unchanged. Static IR supports premature reuse but does not measure hardware execution timestamps. Compilation and post-repair GPU validation are unavailable; repair success is not experimentally verified.","locations":[{"source_id":"source-01","start_line":120,"end_line":135},{"source_id":"source-02","start_line":17,"end_line":26},{"source_id":"source-03","start_line":15,"end_line":24},{"source_id":"source-05","start_line":17,"end_line":26},{"source_id":"source-06","start_line":16,"end_line":22}],"evidence_ids":["case-24","case-25","fact-24","fact-25","fact-26","case-26","case-27","fact-27","fact-28","fact-29","case-30","case-31","fact-33","fact-34","fact-35","case-32","fact-36","fact-37","case-36","fact-42","fact-43"],"edits":[{"old":"  // Merge the alloc liverange with the liverange of any subview of the
